Provenance
------------------------------------------------------------------------------

The decoder and encoder are original implementations written from the AV1
Bitstream & Decoding Process Specification (Alliance for Open Media), in
the text AOMedia publishes (https://aomediacodec.github.io/av1-spec/ and
its source, https://github.com/AOMediaCodec/av1-spec). They are not
translations of, and do not derive from, any other AV1 encoder's or
decoder's source: no implementation's code (libaom, dav1d, rav1d, rav1e,
SVT-AV1, FFmpeg's libavcodec or any other) was read, and none was run in
testing. The specification's tables (default CDFs, scans, quantiser lookups
and matrices, filter taps, block-size and transform-size lookups) are
reproduced from it as data; tools/gen_tables.py extracts them from the
specification's text and regenerates src/tables.rs.

Correctness is checked against data published for decoder testing:

  * AOMedia's AV1 test vectors — bitstreams and the MD5s of their decoded
    frames, from https://storage.googleapis.com/aom-test-data/ — twelve of
    which are included in tests/data (listed in its README);
  * the Argon Streams AV1 conformance streams (v2.1, AOMedia's "AV1 video
    decoder verification tool"), bitstreams and reference MD5s, used from a
    local copy and not distributed with this crate. The suite's coverage
    tool and viewer binaries were not run.

